{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"text","text":"This session is being continued from a previous conversation that ran out of context. The summary below covers the earlier portion of the conversation.\n\nSummary:\n1. Primary Request and Intent:\n   The user (via the cobbler orchestrator) has assigned task #5469: implement srd070 requirements R13.1, R13.2, R13.3, and R13.4 in cmd/fmt. These requirements are about exit codes and differential testing:\n   - R13.1: Exit 0 on successful formatting\n   - R13.2: Exit 1 on invalid option or file open failure\n   - R13.3: Differential tests comparing stdout and exit codes against gfmt reference binary via pkg/testutils\n   - R13.4: Tests must cover all major features: default 75-char formatting, -w width, -g goal, -s split-only, -u uniform spacing, -p prefix, -t tagged paragraph, multi-file input, stdin, blank line paragraphs, indentation preservation, and error cases\n\n   The task specifies modifying `cmd/fmt/main.go` and `cmd/fmt/fmt_test.go` only. Git is managed externally — no git commands allowed.\n\n2. Key Technical Concepts:\n   - Differential testing pattern: `testutils.BuildBinary` + `exec.LookPath(\"gfmt\")` + `testutils.RunDiffTests`\n   - GNU fmt reference binary: `gfmt` installed via Homebrew coreutils\n   - Exit code semantics: 0 for success, 1 for errors (invalid options, missing files)\n   - DiffTest struct: `{Name, Args, Stdin, Env, WorkDir, ExitCode, Normalize, ExpectedFiles}`\n   - The `ExitCode` field in DiffTest defaults to 0; it must be explicitly set for error cases\n   - SIGPIPE handler via `sys.InstallSIGPIPEHandler()`\n   - LC_ALL=C for all differential tests\n\n3. Files and Code Sections:\n   - `docs/specs/software-requirements/srd070-fmt.yaml`\n      - Full SRD defining all fmt requirements R1-R13\n      - R13 group (lines 91-100) defines exit codes and testing requirements\n      - Non-goals: no crown margin mode (-c), no locale-aware line breaking\n   \n   - `cmd/fmt/ma